# The statusline's own menu: a right-click on the row between the
# chips opens *Segments ▸*, every segment ticked while it is shown. A
# row hides its chip at once; the same row shows it again. At 120x40
# with a.txt open the gap sits around column 40 of row 38.
write a.txt "hello\n"
open a.txt
expect screen contains "Ln 1/1 Col 1"
rightclick 40 38
expect screen contains "┌ Statusline"
expect screen contains "Segments"
key right
expect screen contains "Position"
expect screen contains "Clock"
expect screen lacks "RESTRICTED"
# Language is the last built-in row; Position six above it.
key end
key up
key up
key up
key up
key up
key up
key enter
expect screen lacks "Ln 1/1 Col 1"
# And back: the row is unticked now, and the same row restores it.
rightclick 40 38
key right
key end
key up
key up
key up
key up
key up
key up
key enter
expect screen contains "Ln 1/1 Col 1"
